From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Chagas <drochachagas@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 11:18:11 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] Object Selection tool: drag a box around an object to select
 it (AI)

Photoshop's Object Selection tool, first in the W group of the toolbox:
drag a rough box around an object and it becomes the selection. The tool
(GimpObjectSelectTool, a GimpSelectionTool) draws the box while dragging
and, on release, runs GIMPhoto's plug-in procedure gimphoto-object-select
with the box and the tool's selection mode (replace / add / subtract /
intersect, Shift and Ctrl as the other selection tools); the plug-in finds
the object with SAM 2.1 on the local ComfyUI. Its message is shown when
that fails (no local AI, ComfyUI not answering). Moving the selection with
the usual modifiers works as with the other selection tools.

